From: Towfienes <ngolamtien1706@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:43:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] hyprvx: vendor CameraMath and add per-monitor camera state

Patch 0001 of the HyprVX V3 series (Feature 001, Sprint 1).

- src/hyprvx/CameraMath.hpp: byte-identical copy of HyprVX
  core/include/hyprvx/core/CameraMath.hpp (BSD-3-Clause), the single
  world <-> screen transform (contract v1.1).
- src/hyprvx/MonitorCamera.{hpp,cpp}: per-monitor camera (origin, zoom,
  revision). Inactive means identityFor(M) and follows the monitor
  origin exactly. setCamera validates against the MVP zoom range
  0.1 ... 2.0 and leaves the state unchanged (and logs) on rejection;
  every change increments the revision. resetCamera restores exact
  identity.
- CMonitor gains one member, m_hyprvxCamera.

No render, input or damage change: nothing reads the camera yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
